
= Forth for TIC-80 =

A port of the Forth language (based on pforth) as a scripting language for
TIC-80, the fantasy console for making, playing and sharing tiny retro
games. Adds Forth to the list of available cartridge languages, alongside
Lua, JavaScript, Ruby, and others.

[images/tic80-forth.png]

https://github.com/luginf/TIC-80

= Halebarde et Gonfanon =

A turn-based strategy game in pygame, adapted from the board game of the same
name. Two kingdoms face each other on a bounded battlefield: mail-clad
soldiers, archers, and scouts able to infiltrate the enemy camp. Two players
locally or over the network, or against an AI at three levels, with three
graphical themes.

[images/halebarde.png]

[github.com/luginf/halebarde_et_gonfanon https://github.com/luginf/halebarde_et_gonfanon]

= Tic-tac-toe for Uxn =

Two tic-tac-toe games for Hundredrabbits' [Varvara/Uxn https://wiki.xxiivv.com/site/uxntal.html]
virtual machine: a 3x3 grid and a 5x5 grid where you need four in a row. Playable
with the mouse or the keyboard.

[images/uxn-xo.png]

[github.com/luginf/uxneries https://github.com/luginf/uxneries]
